\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A grading built from the operator}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{With exact anticommutation, applying the Dirac operator to
a positive grading vector produces a negative grading vector or
zero. A quadratic term changes this exchange. On a zero mode
the product #{\Gamma(\bbI-aD)} acts just as #{\Gamma} does,
while on a vector with #{Dv=2a^{-1}v} its action is reversed.
When does this product supply two orthogonal grading spaces
on the whole carrier?}
